{
	"info": {
		"name": "TaskOrbit API",
		"description": "Test collection for the TaskOrbit backend (Express + Prisma).\n\n**Setup**\n1. Start the server (`PORT=5000` from `.env`). Base URL variable: `{{baseUrl}}` = `http://localhost:5000/api/v1`.\n2. Auth tokens are issued as **HttpOnly cookies** (`access_token`, `refresh_token`) — never in the response body. Postman's cookie jar stores them automatically on Login / Verify-Email / Refresh, and sends them on every later request. Keep the cookie jar enabled.\n3. **Token capture on login:** outside production the Login response returns both tokens in the body as `data.access_token` / `data.refresh_token`. Its post-response script runs ONLY when the response is `success: true` with a login-success message, then writes both tokens into the collection variables `access_token` and `refresh_token`, and the collection-level pre-request script attaches `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>` to every following request. A failed login (`success: false`) stores nothing.\n4. Fallback: you can also paste a JWT into `access_token` by hand. Leave it empty before logging in to rely on cookies alone.\n5. Flow: Register → Verify Email (OTP from mail/Redis) → Login → use the rest. Fill `{{projectId}}`, `{{taskId}}`, `{{commentId}}`, `{{userId}}`, `{{memberId}}`, `{{attachmentId}}`, `{{notificationId}}`, `{{contactId}}`, `{{invitationToken}}`, `{{sessionId}}` as you discover real IDs.\n\n**Roles**\n- `ADMIN` — seeded admin account (see `src/app/utils/seed.ts`).\n- `PROJECT_MANAGER` — creates projects/tasks, invites members.\n- `TEAM_MEMBER` — comments, attachments, status moves, invitations.\n- Any authenticated user can hit routes guarded by `auth()` with no role.\n\nA collection-level test asserts no 5xx on every request.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"event": [
		{
			"listen": "prerequest",
			"script": {
				"type": "text/javascript",
				"exec": [
					"// Optional header-auth fallback: only sent when access_token is non-empty.",
					"const t = pm.collectionVariables.get('access_token');",
					"if (t) {",
					"\tpm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Authorization', value: 'Bearer ' + t });",
					"}"
				]
			}
		},
		{
			"listen": "test",
			"script": {
				"type": "text/javascript",
				"exec": [
					"pm.test('No 5xx server error', function () {",
					"\tpm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.below(500);",
					"});",
					"// Mirror the session cookie into access_token so it also works as a header fallback.",
					"try {",
					"\tconst c = pm.cookies.get('access_token');",
					"\tif (c) pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', (c && c.value) ? c.value : c);",
					"} catch (e) {}"
				]
			}
		}
	],
	"variable": [
		{ "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:5000/api/v1" },
		{ "key": "serverUrl", "value": "http://localhost:5000" },
		{ "key": "access_token", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "refresh_token", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "email", "value": "tester@example.com" },
		{ "key": "password", "value": "Password123" },
		{ "key": "otp", "value": "123456" },
		{ "key": "google_id_token", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "userId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "projectId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "taskId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "commentId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "attachmentId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "notificationId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "contactId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "memberId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "invitationToken", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "sessionId", "value": "" }
	],
